title: 'Migrate `disputes::slashing` from the deprecated `ValidateUnsigned` trait to `#[pallet::authorize]`'

doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    `polkadot-runtime-parachains::disputes::slashing` no longer uses the deprecated
    `ValidateUnsigned` trait and the `#[pallet::validate_unsigned]` attribute. The validation of
    `report_dispute_lost_unsigned` moved to a `#[pallet::authorize]` callback.

    The validation semantics do not change. The callback accepts only `TransactionSource::Local` and
    `TransactionSource::InBlock`, it runs the same staleness check, and it builds the same
    transaction validity. The public `Pallet::validate_unsigned` and `Pallet::pre_dispatch` helpers
    are gone, because `pre_dispatch` ran the same check as `validate_unsigned`.

    Two changes affect a runtime that includes this pallet. The `SlashingReportHandler` bound changed
    from `CreateBare<Call<T>>` to `CreateAuthorizedTransaction<Call<T>>`, and the runtime must put
    `frame_system::AuthorizeCall` in its transaction extension pipeline. A runtime that forgets
    `AuthorizeCall` still compiles, but the report never gets an authorized origin, so unsigned
    dispute slashing stops working.

    `weight_of_authorize` charges the existing `report_dispute_lost_unsigned` weight. Authorization
    repeats the session check and the key ownership proof check that the dispatch also does, so the
    dispatch weight is a safe upper bound.

crates:
- name: polkadot-runtime-parachains
  bump: major
- name: pallet-staking-async-rc-runtime
  bump: major
